  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Do you know Professor Saeed? He is the algorithms professor at Damascus University. Yesterday, he gave his students hard homework (he is known for being so evil) - for a given binary string SSS, they should compute the sum of F(S,L,R)F(S, L, R)F(S,L,R) over all pairs of integers (L,R)(L, R)(L,R) (1≤L≤R≤∣S∣1 \\le L \\le R \\le |S|1≤L≤R≤∣S∣), where the function F(S,L,R)F(S, L, R)F(S,L,R) is defined as follows:\n\n\nCreate a string UUU: first, set U=SU = SU=S, and for each iii (L≤i≤RL \\le i \\le RL≤i≤R), flip the iii-th character of UUU (change '1' to '0' or '0' to '1').\nThen, F(S,L,R)F(S, L, R)F(S,L,R) is the number of valid pairs (i,i+1)(i, i + 1)(i,i+1) such that Ui=Ui+1U_i = U_{i+1}Ui​=Ui+1​.\nAs usual, Professor Saeed will give more points to efficient solutions. Please help the students solve this homework.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤∣S∣≤3⋅1061 \\le |S| \\le 3 \\cdot 10^61≤∣S∣≤3⋅106",
      "the sum of ∣S∣|S|∣S∣ over all test cases does not exceed 6⋅1066 \\cdot 10^66⋅106",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (50 points):**",
      "1≤∣S∣≤3001 \\le |S| \\le 3001≤∣S∣≤300",
      "the sum of ∣S∣|S|∣S∣ over all test cases does not exceed 600600600"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single string SSS.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ∑1≤L≤R≤∣S∣F(S,L,R)\\sum_{1 \\le L \\le R \\le |S|} F(S, L, R)∑1≤L≤R≤∣S∣​F(S,L,R).",
    "notes": [],
